      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        306.17193603515625,
        527.433837890625,
        320.6149597167969
      ],
      "text": "with regimens containing a rifamycin (rifampicin or rifapentine). IPT has been the most widely used",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        319.3719177246094,
        527.14697265625,
        333.81494140625
      ],
      "text": "form of TPT, but the shorter duration of rifamycin regimens presents a clear advantage, making these",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.988594055175781,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        332.5718078613281,
        527.408203125,
        347.01483154296875
      ],
      "text": "regimens increasingly preferred. TPT for MDR/RR-TB requires a different approach, primarily with",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        345.7718200683594,
